**Definition 6.1 (coefficient maps and the retained optimization).** In
unnormalized output-input vectorization put
$\mathcal V=(|D\rangle\!\rangle,|T\rangle\!\rangle,|S\rangle\!\rangle)$.
Its columns are independent and orthogonal, but not normalized. For a
Hermitian coefficient matrix $Z$ define

$$
\Lambda_Z(A)=\sum_{i,j}Z_{ij}K_iAK_j^\dagger,\qquad
\Theta(Z)=\sum_{i,j}Z_{ij}K_j^\dagger K_i,\qquad (K_D,K_T,K_S)=(D,T,S).
\tag{CA.26}
$$

Then $J_{\Lambda_Z}=\mathcal VZ\mathcal V^\dagger$ and the actual input
effect is $\Theta(Z)$; $\operatorname{Tr}_{\rm out}J_{\Lambda_Z}=
\Theta(Z)^T$. In particular $\Theta(I)=I-M$, and $\Theta$ preserves
positive order. Let $\mathcal K_s$ consist of

$$
\begin{gathered}
H_+,H_-\succeq0,\qquad L_+,L_-\in\mathcal C_2,\qquad
H_++H_-+L_++L_-=I_3,\\
0\preceq N:=\frac{I_3+s\kappa X_{01}}2-\Theta(H_++L_+)\preceq M.
\end{gathered}
\tag{CA.27}
$$

The original resource quantity remains

$$
\mathsf E_s(\rho)=\min_{\mathcal K_s}
 \operatorname{tr}(\Theta(H_++H_-)\rho),\qquad \rho\succeq0.
\tag{CA.28}
$$

This is IR's retained exact finite problem, distinct from the error
$\mathcal E_*$. In (CA.27) each low membership can now be expressed by
Theorem 4.3. The plane slack is still a variable.

